# npm 7+ auto-installs peerDependencies. React must not be installed here.
#
# Consumers link this package from a sibling checkout, and Node resolves a
# linked package's imports from its *real* path -- so a react/ under this repo
# becomes a second React copy in the consuming app, which breaks hooks and
# context in ways that are hard to trace back here.
#
# omit=peer skips installing the peers without touching the peerDependencies
# field itself. That field has to stay: rollup builds its `external` list from
# dependencies + peerDependencies, and losing the entry would silently bundle
# React into dist/.
omit=peer
